 "answer": "The `vector` type in pgvector supports up to **16,000 dimensions**.\n\nThis is a limit on the column type itself. Indexes have lower limits: HNSW and IVFFlat indexes on `vector` columns support up to 2,000 dimensions. For higher-dimensional embeddings, you can use `halfvec` (up to 16,000 dimensions for storage, with indexes up to 4,000) or binary quantization.\n\nI'm answering from general knowledge of pgvector, not from your project's code or documentation. Check the pgvector version you're running, since these limits have changed across releases.",
